{
 "id": "sd-learning-curve-truth",
 "name": "SD: A support team that learns on the job: the truth",
 "description": "Tests an effect shaped like a learning curve. Support tickets are answered at a rate proportional to the backlog, times an effect of the team's experience: a table sampled from 0.2 + 0.8 x (1 - (1 - 0.5)^(experience / 400)), so a new team works at 0.2 of full speed and productivity saturates as experience grows. Experience grows with the work done (0.5 practice points per ticket answered: the same equation and effect as answering) and decays 2.0% a day (forgetting, staff turnover); an announced era (a reorganisation) makes it decay faster for a while, so the team's productivity falls and the backlog rises. Demand changes without notice. Some tickets go to engineering (not measured) and come back answered; some answers are reopened.",
 "time_unit": "day",
